## SQ-PTH-24 | IE revolver shot and Blocky Siege cannon ball pass a cube at full speed; snowball breaks in the centre
@group A
@commands 3x3x3 cobweb cube: `/summon immersiveengineering:revolver_shot` and `blocky_siege:projectile_cannon_ball_projectile_projectile` aimed through it (`Motion:[1.5d,0d,0d]`), then a snowball the same way
@pass both munitions leave the far side at the same speed; the snowball breaks in the centre
@fails IE shots extend AbstractArrow: without the exempt tag they hang; `PassProjectiles.groupOf` reads `passthrough_exempt/all` first
@from batches/r1115/pth_a1.qb
> fill 1010 -60 1179 1012 -58 1181 minecraft:cobweb
> summon immersiveengineering:revolver_shot 1004.5 -58.5 1180.5 {NoGravity:1b,Tags:["m24a"]}
> zpth watch m24a 45 1
> zpth launch m24a none 1.5 0 0
sleep 2
> summon blocky_siege:projectile_cannon_ball_projectile_projectile 1004.5 -58.5 1180.5 {NoGravity:1b,Tags:["m24b"]}
> zpth watch m24b 45 1
> zpth launch m24b none 1.5 0 0
sleep 2
> summon minecraft:snowball 1004.5 -58.5 1180.5 {NoGravity:1b,Tags:["m24c"]}
> zpth watch m24c 45 1
> zpth launch m24c none 1.5 0 0
sleep 2
look m24a / m24b: x passes 1013 with mot x about 1.5 (ng off: gravity drop allowed); m24c gone near x 1011.5


@@section 5
@@title SQ-PTH Pass-through blocks, phase 6 (benchmark, perf suite, timing log), 2026-11-15 ([plan_passthrough.md](../plan_passthrough.md) 7)
@@date 2026-11-15
@@jars creativecompat creativedevtools
@@sources feature_writeup/plan_passthrough.md
@@text
@@text Creative Compat 1.0.0 and Creative Devtools 1.0.0 built 2026-11-15 00:40 (build/libs, not installed); both jars in
@@text `srv/mods` (Devtools is dev-only: `/cdevbench`, `pbot`). The Compat jar carries the phase 4 tags, so no datapack. Run
@@text these after SQ-PTH-19 (tags load). Budget (plan 7.2): micro under 1000 ns per entity-tick in the field and the web
@@text cube; macro under 0.5 ms added mean tick time at 500 affected entities.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-PTH-25 | /cdevbench passthrough (default and 200000 calls): 10 cases, tagged, enabled, medians, json, fixtures removed
@group A
@commands Op player (or bot) in a loaded area, view distance 4+; `/cdevbench passthrough`; then `/cdevbench passthrough 200000`; read `kubejs/exported/perf/passthrough_bench.json`; look at the build limit above the player afterwards
@pass chat lists 10 cases with ns per call, `tagged=true`, `enabled=true`; `tick_field` and `tick_web_cube` medians under 1000 ns (green); `tick_air` the lowest of the tick cases; json has `cases` with `median_ns`, `p99_ns`; no fixture blocks left at the build limit; the server did not hit the watchdog
@fails `tagged=false`: Compat jar without the tags; red medians: record them in blockrunner.md 3.10 (caching per plan 7.2 is the next step, owner call); blocks left: the restore loop in `PassBenchCommand.bench`
@from batches/r1115/pth_a2.qb
> tp P 1060.5 -60 1060.5
> execute as P at P run cdevbench passthrough
waitlog \[cdevbench\] passthrough: .* calls per case 300
> execute as P at P run cdevbench passthrough 200000
waitlog \[cdevbench\] passthrough: 200000 calls per case 300
shell python3 -c "import json;d=json.load(open('kubejs/exported/perf/passthrough_bench.json'));print({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k!='cases'});[print(c) for c in (d['cases'] if isinstance(d['cases'],list) else [dict(name=k,**v) for k,v in d['cases'].items()])]"
> fill 1042 300 1042 1078 319 1078 minecraft:air replace minecraft:wheat
> fill 1042 300 1042 1078 319 1078 minecraft:air replace minecraft:cobweb
> fill 1042 300 1042 1078 319 1078 minecraft:air replace minecraft:carrots
> fill 1042 300 1042 1078 319 1078 minecraft:air replace minecraft:farmland
> fill 1042 300 1042 1078 319 1078 minecraft:air replace minecraft:stone
> fill 1042 300 1042 1078 319 1078 minecraft:air replace minecraft:dirt
expect \[cdevbench\]
reject Successfully filled
look chat (console) 10 cases, tagged=true enabled=true; tick_field and tick_web_cube median < 1000 ns; tick_air lowest tick case; json cases median_ns p99_ns; no watchdog

## SQ-PTH-26 | enabled false: no modifier, vanilla web crawl, bench enabled false; true: modifier back
@group A
@commands `/cdevbench passthrough enabled false`; read `config/creativecompat-common.toml` `[surface.passthrough] enabled`; zombie in a lone web: read the pass-through modifier (`/attribute ... modifier value get a1386f64-4583-4798-9b29-f040c59b8574`) and `/data get entity ... Motion`; `/cdevbench passthrough` once; `/cdevbench passthrough enabled true`
@pass file says false and back to true; with false: no pass-through modifier, the zombie crawls as in vanilla (stuck slowdown back), the bench json says `enabled: false` and its tick cases are near `tick_air`; with true: modifier -0.5 again
@fails `PassValues.refresh` not reached (modifier stays); the file watcher reload re-sends twice (harmless)
@from batches/r1115/pth_a2.qb
> execute as P at P run cdevbench passthrough enabled false
sleep 2
shell grep -nE '^\s*enabled' config/creativecompat-common.toml | sed -n '1,12p'; awk '/\[surface\.passthrough\]/{f=1} f&&/enabled/{print; exit}' config/creativecompat-common.toml
> setblock 1000 -60 1070 minecraft:cobweb
> setblock 1010 -60 1078 minecraft:cobweb
> summon minecraft:zombie 1000.5 -60 1070.5 {Tags:["z26a"],PersistenceRequired:1b,IsBaby:0b,CanPickUpLoot:0b,Attributes:[{Name:"minecraft:generic.movement_speed",Base:0d}]}
> summon minecraft:zombie 1006.5 -60 1078.5 {Tags:["z26m"],PersistenceRequired:1b,IsBaby:0b,CanPickUpLoot:0b,Attributes:[{Name:"minecraft:generic.movement_speed",Base:0d}]}
sleep 1
> zpth mod z26a
> zpth watch z26m 160 4
repeat 12
> zpth motion z26m 0.25 0 0
end
sleep 2
> execute as P at P run cdevbench passthrough
waitlog \[cdevbench\] passthrough: .* calls per case 300
shell python3 -c "import json;d=json.load(open('kubejs/exported/perf/passthrough_bench.json'));print('enabled',d.get('enabled'));print(d['cases'])" | cut -c1-2000
> execute as P at P run cdevbench passthrough enabled true
sleep 2
shell awk '/\[surface\.passthrough\]/{f=1} f&&/enabled/{print; exit}' config/creativecompat-common.toml
> zpth mod z26a
> kill @e[tag=z26m]
look file false then true; z26a mod=none while false, -0.500 after true; z26m pushed: stops in the web at x 1010 (vanilla stuck) unlike SQ-PTH-02r; bench json enabled false, tick cases near tick_air

## SQ-PTH-27 | [debug.passthrough] timing true (set before boot): herd in a 9x9 wheat field plus 20 items in a web; parser; key false stops lines
@group A
@commands `qrun.py toml config/creativecompat-common.toml debug.passthrough timing true` before boot; boot; a zombie herd in a 9x9 wheat field (age 7) and 20 items in webs; 60 s; `python3 tools/perf/passthrough_timing.py srv/logs/latest.log`; then set the key false and save while running, wait 30 s
@pass `[passthrough-timing] side=server ticks=200 ...` every 10 s; the parser prints a server block with share of tick time, `inside` about the herd plus items per tick, `counts` above 0; no new lines 10 s after the key went false; no `side=client` line on a dedicated server
@fails no lines: `PassTiming.on` never set (tick listener not registered) or the key path differs; inside 0: `PassTiming.hook` reads the state after `leave` reset it
